& [RuntimeBoundaryMap: FSC3RuntimeBoundaryAndInvariantMapV1] is the imported runtime boundary map for FSC3 runtime graph proof
  + [slice_id] is FSC3-S01
  + [source_chunk] is FSC2 planning coordination
  + [target_chunk] is FSC3 runtime graph proof
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is docs/planning/FSC2_Planning_Coordination_Pack.v1.sop
  + [accepted_boundary_input_sha256] is 488028EFDB7178A0AEB329F5689A915B86AFF52CB445E3BFB1D0D29581626B76
  + [import_policy] is read_only_import
  + [runtime_policy] is runtime graph contracts may consume accepted packets and operator contracts but cannot become source authority
  + [implementation_policy] is no executable runtime graph implementation is authorized by this map alone

  = must: treat FSC1 and FSC2 packs as accepted boundary inputs, not editable runtime drafts
  = must: treat LangGraph checkpoints as execution state, not authority
  = must: route authority conflict, ambiguous identity, stale input, missing proof, contested claim, high-risk operation, and human override through SOP-first interrupt
  - never: let graph state, checkpoint state, or node output silently mutate source authority

& [ImportedRuntimeContractInventory] is the accepted contract inventory imported into FSC3
  + [imported_pack] is FSC1FoundationContractPackV1
  + [imported_pack] is FSC2PlanningCoordinationPackV1
  + [imported_contract] is planning_readiness_recompute v1
  + [imported_contract] is work_packet_generation v1
  + [imported_contract] is coordination_claim_register v1
  + [imported_contract] is coordination_conflict_signal v1
  + [imported_contract] is completion_review_delta_gate v1
  + [imported_contract] is OperatorTraceSchema
  + [imported_contract] is RendezvousPacketContract
  + [imported_fixture_plan] is FSC2PlanningCoordinationFixturePlanV1

  = must: preserve accepted input and output record-kind constraints from imported contracts
  = must: preserve support_delta, requirement_delta, stale trigger, coordination claim, and completion review obligations

& [RuntimeOwnedInvariantSet] is the invariant set owned by FSC3
  + [invariant] is graph state is execution state only
  + [invariant] is checkpoint state is execution state only
  + [invariant] is SOP files and accepted packs remain the source of truth
  + [invariant] is graph nodes may only perform duties represented by accepted operator contracts
  + [invariant] is every graph node path emits operator_trace or preserves an existing trace reference
  + [invariant] is success, blocked, stale, fault, and interrupt outcomes remain distinguishable
  + [invariant] is SOP-first interrupt pauses graph mutation until accepted resume condition exists
  + [invariant] is contested coordination claims block packet execution paths
  + [invariant] is completion_review_delta_gate remains the only accepted next-gate control contract
  + [invariant] is runtime outputs consumed by future surfaces must be traceable to accepted packets and operator traces

  = must: preserve these invariants through FSC3-S02 through FSC3-S06
  = must: mark downstream FSC3 slices stale when any invariant changes

& [CheckpointAuthorityBoundary] is the authority boundary for runtime checkpoints
  + [checkpoint_role] is pause and resume execution state
  + [checkpoint_role] is preserve graph-local state for runtime continuation
  + [checkpoint_not_role] is source authority
  + [checkpoint_not_role] is accepted decision
  + [checkpoint_not_role] is completion review
  + [checkpoint_not_role] is coordination claim acceptance
  + [checkpoint_not_role] is proof result unless separately emitted as proof_result

  = must: reject any graph contract that treats checkpoint state as signed_sjs, proof_backed, or accepted_decision authority
  = must: require lineage from checkpoint outputs back to accepted operator traces and source authority

& [ForbiddenRuntimeMutationList: FSC3] is the forbidden mutation set for FSC3-S01
  + [forbidden_mutation] is editing accepted FSC1 or FSC2 output files to make runtime proof easier
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating checkpoint state as authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating graph state as authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing executable LangGraph nodes
  + [forbidden_mutation] is installing runtime packages
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing checkpoint persistence
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing surface adapters
  + [forbidden_mutation] is dispatching real work
  + [forbidden_mutation] is authorizing operations control
  + [forbidden_mutation] is omitting operator_trace on graph path output

  = must: fail FSC3-S01 review if any forbidden mutation appears in the output

& [DownstreamStaleTriggerList: FSC3] is the stale trigger set for FSC3 downstream work
  + [stale_trigger] is FSC2 planning coordination pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is FSC3 final slice surface changes
  + [stale_trigger] is runtime boundary invariant changes
  + [stale_trigger] is graph contract changes after interrupt contract work starts
  + [stale_trigger] is interrupt contract changes after trace proof work starts
  + [stale_trigger] is trace proof contract changes after fixture planning starts
  + [stale_trigger] is imported operator contract changes
  + [stale_trigger] is false-ready checkpoint or checkpoint authority confusion is detected
  + [stale_trigger] is hidden graph write or missing operator_trace is detected

  = must: mark affected downstream slices stale when any listed trigger fires
  = must: route stale-trigger repair through completion review rather than silent edits

& [FSC3S01AcceptanceChecklist] is the verification checklist for FSC3-S01
  + [required_component] is imported runtime contract inventory
  + [required_component] is runtime-owned invariant set
  + [required_component] is checkpoint authority boundary
  + [required_component] is forbidden runtime mutation list
  + [required_component] is downstream stale trigger list
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is runtime graph implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is checkpoint persistence implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is package installation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is surface implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is operations control

  = must: accept FSC3-S01 only when runtime imports are mapped without creating implementation authority
